==Battleground==
*10 [[Znache]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*7 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Dagshund]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Prof. Owlbrowley]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 160 seconds<sup>4,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Zyclone]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Shachiko]] spawns after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.
*1 [[Zyclone]] spawns after 126.67 seconds<sup>3,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A simple yet challenging Zombie stage. Most threats are spawned independently of one another, allowing you to handle them at a leisurely pace.

Kill the Dagshund at the start—preferably with [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train]] for the Double Bounty bonus. By the time you're finished, the first Prof. Owlbrowley will make its appearance. A few well-timed [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] will turn the scholar into freshly cooked fowl.

At this point, use generic Zombie counters like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]], and [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] to both crowd-control and damage the first Zyclone. Well timed [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cats]] will render Relic Doges and Znaches a non-issue for the most part; [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] can also use Zyclone as a stepping stone to snipe the second Dagshund. Once Shachiko makes its way to your front lines, take care of the remaining peons in the field, then lure them to your Cat Base and promptly jump it with [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]]. Although the remaining enemy units will arrive dangerously close to your Cat Base, the cleanup phase should not be too difficult with the money dropped by Shachiko.

The second Prof. Owlbrowley won't be able to do much on their own, a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can use the Zyclones as a stepping stone to launch devastating [[Wave Attack]]s which severely cripple it. Otherwise, a combination of Fishman Cats and Bullet Trains timed between Zyclone knockbacks will do the trick. Once Prof. Owlbrowley dies, you have essentially beaten the stage.

==Trivia==
*Like most [[Forest Playground]] stages, Broadleaf Yo-Yo's name is a reference to a toy. In this case, Broadleaf Yo-Yo refers to [[wikipedia:Yo-yo|yo-yos]], which can be made out of wood such as that of a [[wikipedia:Broadleaf|broadleaf tree]].

